{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_3wk4x2bsshuskvbuifjqeyc6ftymzuagk3byi64fmo3thstbtbda","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The translation is complete and verified.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src/` is a single-module library (`CMakeLists.txt`, `include/lib.h`, `src/lib.c` — 104 lines total): a trimmed-down version of the `cute_c2` 2D collision detection routines, with `collided()` as the public dispatch entry point.\n\n## Files written (in the current directory, not `c_src/`)\n\n- **`Cargo.toml`** — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`, crate named `translated_rust` so the output is `libtranslated_rust.so`, matching the C build (CMake derives the project name from the parent directory).\n- **`src/lib.rs`** — full translation: 3 `#[repr(C)]` structs (`c2v`, `c2Circle`, `c2AABB`) and all 10 functions with `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] extern \"C\"`.\n\nNo namespace-renaming macros exist in the header, so linker names equal source names.\n\n## Completion gate: symbol diff is empty\n\n| | Symbols |\n|---|---|\n| C `.so` | 10 |\n| Rust `.so` | 10 |\n| Missing from Rust | **none** |\n\n`c2V`, `c2Maxv`, `c2Minv`, `c2Clampv`, `c2Sub`, `c2Dot`, `c2CircletoCircle`, `c2CircletoAABB`, `c2AABBtoAABB`, `collided`. The Rust `.so` exports *exactly* these and nothing extra — no leaked Rust runtime symbols.\n\n## Behavioral verification\n\nI wrote a differential harness that `dlopen`s both the C and Rust `.so` files and compares every function bit-for-bit (`memcmp` on returned structs/floats, not `==`) across a value pool including `NaN`, `±0.0`, `±Infinity`, denormals, and huge magnitudes:\n\n**3,365,388 checks, 0 mismatches.**\n\nThis also exercises the by-value struct ABI (`c2v` returned in `xmm0`; `c2Circle`/`c2AABB` passed across SSE register pairs), confirming `repr(C)` matches the SysV C ABI.\n\n## C semantics deliberately preserved\n\n- **`c2Maxv`/`c2Minv`**: used raw `if a.x > b.x { a.x } else { b.x }` rather than `f32::max`/`f32::min`. This matters — Rust's `max`/`min` return the *non-NaN* operand, whereas the C ternary yields a false comparison on NaN and selects `b`. Using `f32::max` would have silently diverged on NaN inputs.\n- **`c2AABBtoAABB`**: reproduced the four `int` flags combined with bitwise `|` then logically negated, rather than simplifying to boolean `&&` logic.\n- **`collided`**: preserved the nested-`switch` check order and the `return 0` fallthrough for unrecognized `C2_TYPE` tags (tested with tags `2`, `-1`, `7`). The `typeA == AABB, typeB == CIRCLE` branch swapping its arguments into `c2CircletoAABB(B, A)` was carried over as-is.\n- **`c2Dot`**: left as plain `a.x * b.x + a.y * b.y`; no FMA contraction, matching the default x86-64 target which has no FMA enabled.\n\nOne safety note: `collided` reads shapes out of `*const c_void` via `read_unaligned`, which is behaviorally identical to the C casts for aligned data but avoids UB if a caller ever passes an under-aligned pointer.\n\n`cargo build --release` compiles cleanly with no warnings."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":704,"cache_read_input_tokens":25670,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":704,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5f6baa1-b348-4eb5-8004-8efff66e62ab","uuid":"6e5370ac-b586-4d87-8eac-124834fd39c3","timestamp":"2026-08-18T15:03:14.705Z"}
